{"sections":[{"type":"Meta","title":"Bristol's employment, unemployment and economic inactivity - ONS","description":"How Bristol (E06000023) compares with the South West and Great Britain across employment-related statistics","contentTitle":"Labour market robo reports","releaseDate":"20240514","lastUpdated":"2024-05-14","outputSeries":"labourmarketindicatorsbyunitaryandlocalauthoritiesgreatbritain","contentType":"robo-journalism"},{"type":"Header","title":"Employment, unemployment and economic inactivity in Bristol","standfirst":"How Bristol compares with the South West and Great Britain across employment-related statistics","label":"Select a different local authority"},{"type":"Notice","content":"<p>This pilot publication is no longer being updated. Feedback to help us develop future publications can be sent to our <a href = \"mailto: subnational@ons.gov.uk\">subnational analysis team</a>.</p>"},{"id":"section-top","type":"Summary","title":"In Bristol:","content":"<a name=\"section-top\"></a>","sections":[{"indicator":"Employment rate","value":"76.1%","note":"ages 16 to 64","content":"<p>Employment in Bristol has decreased compared with the previous year. Bristol's employment rate was lower than across the South West as a whole in the year ending December 2023.</p><p><a href=\"#employment-rate\">Go to employment rate section</a>  &darr;</p>"},{"indicator":"Unemployment rate","value":"3.6%","note":"ages 16+","content":"<p>Unemployment (people looking for work) has risen since a year earlier. The unemployment rate for Bristol was higher than across the South West as a whole.</p><p><a href=\"#unemployment\">Go to unemployment rate section</a>  &darr;</p>"},{"indicator":"Claimant Count","value":"3.6%","note":"ages 16 to 64","content":"<p>Claimant Count was higher in March 2024 compared with a year earlier. The <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/aguidetolabourmarketstatistics#claimant-count\" rel=\"external\">Claimant Count</a>  measures the number of people who are claiming unemployment-related benefits.         </p><p><a href=\"#claimant-count\">Go to Claimant Count section</a>  &darr;</p>"},{"indicator":"Economic inactivity","value":"20.8%","note":"ages 16 to 64","content":"<p>Economic inactivity has increased since the previous year. These are people who are neither employed nor seeking work.</p><p><a href=\"#inactivity\">Go to economic inactivity section</a>  &darr;</p>"}]},{"id":"caveat","type":"Warning","content":"<p> These estimates are less precise than national or regional figures because they are based on smaller numbers of survey respondents.</p><p> Local population changes also mean that the numbers of people in each area who are employed, unemployed and economically inactive in this article may be under- or over-estimates.</p>"},{"type":"survey","content":"<p>Estimates of employment and economic inactivity are based on the <a href= \"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/methodologies/annualpopulationsurveyapsqmi\" rel=\"external\">Annual Population Survey</a>. Unemployment estimates are modelled to improve their precision compared to those based only on responses provided via the Annual Population Survey.</p><p>The Claimant Count is based on administrative data from the benefits system. These data are experimental statistics.</p>"},{"id":"employment-rate","title":"Employment in Bristol has decreased compared with the previous year","content":"<p>Bristol's employment rate was lower than across the South West as a whole in the year ending December 2023.</p><p>Of people aged 16 to 64 years living in Bristol, 76.1% were employed in the year ending December 2023. This is a decrease compared with the year ending December 2022 when the local rate was 78.5%.</p><p>Across the South West in the year ending December 2023, 78.8% of people aged 16 to 64 years were employed. This was slightly higher compared with the previous year, when 78.3% of people were employed.</p>"},{"id":"chart-timeseries","type":"Chart","chartType":"line-highlight","title":"Employment rates of areas in the South West","subtitle":"Among those aged 16 to 64 years (%), year ending December 2013 to year ending December 2023","footer":"Source: Annual Population Survey from the Office for National Statistics","data":[{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2013","y":70.2},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2014","y":70.9},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2015","y":76.2},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2016","y":75.6},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2017","y":78.2},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2018","y":77.1},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2019","y":76.7},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2020","y":77.2},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2021","y":78},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2022","y":78.5},{"z":"Bristol, City of","x":"2023","y":76.1},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2013","y":70.1},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2014","y":72.7},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2015","y":73.6},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2016","y":73.8},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2017","y":74.7},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2018","y":75.8},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2019","y":74},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2020","y":75.7},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2021","y":75.4},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2022","y":73.6},{"z":"Plymouth","x":"2023","y":72.9},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2013","y":72.3},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2014","y":79.9},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2015","y":82.1},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2016","y":66.4},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2017","y":79.9},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2018","y":73.6},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2019","y":77.5},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2020","y":76.2},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2021","y":77.4},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2022","y":70.4},{"z":"Exeter","x":"2023","y":78.8},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2013","y":76.8},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2014","y":74.8},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2015","y":73.8},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2016","y":79.8},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2017","y":84.6},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2018","y":81.2},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2019","y":84.3},{"z":"Cheltenham","x":"2020","y":77.1},{"z":"Chelte